# CLAUDE.md — Full Service Pros Team Defaults

> Global instructions for all Claude Code sessions.
> Maintained centrally by Mark. Run `claude-update` to get the latest version.

---

## 1. Who you are working with

You are assisting a Full Service Pros team member. Assume business context:
professional services, client deliverables, operational efficiency. Default to
concise, action-oriented responses. No filler. No preambles.

## 2. Response style

- Terse. The user can read the output — skip trailing summaries.
- Bullet lists only for 3+ parallel items; otherwise prose.
- Cite sources when using MCP/file data: `[Title](URL)` format.

## 3. Tooling defaults

- Use dedicated MCPs before falling back to browser or shell.
- Use `Grep` / `Glob` / `Read` — never `bash grep/find/cat`.
- Use subagents for research and parallel analysis; keep main context clean.

## 4. Task approach

- Plan before acting on any task with 3+ steps.
- Never mark a task complete without demonstrating it works.
- Fix bugs at the root cause — no temporary patches.
- Only touch code that is necessary for the task. No side-effect changes.

## 5. When to pause

Only stop and ask when:
- You need information only the user has (credential, product decision).
- The action executes a financial transaction.
- The action is irreversible and affects shared systems outside this project.

Otherwise: proceed, execute, report what you did.

## 6. Output quality — automatic

A `UserPromptSubmit` hook injects FSP output standards before every response.
You do not need to do anything — quality guidance is applied automatically.

To get an explicitly optimised prompt for a complex task, say:
> "optimise this prompt: [your request]"

Or invoke `/prompt-optimize` directly.

Available skill shortcuts worth knowing:
- `/prompt-optimize` — rewrites a vague request into a precise, high-output prompt
- `/skill-optimizer` — audits how well a skill performed after an agent run
- `/code-review` — review any code change before shipping
- `/gsd-do` — plan + execute a multi-step task end-to-end

## 7. Shared Brain — check before every client task

FSP runs a shared knowledge base accessible to all staff. All memories, decisions,
research, communications, and session activity are stored there and queryable by anyone.

**Before starting any client task:**
- Call `fsp_get_client_context("[client name]")` — returns full history, active projects,
  recent communications, open decisions, and what the team has been working on
- Call `fsp_recall("[topic]")` — semantic search across all past research and outputs

**After completing significant work:**
- Call `fsp_log_activity("[2–3 sentence summary]")` — this session logged to team record
- For any decision made: call `fsp_remember(content, type="decision", client="...")`
- For research findings: call `fsp_remember(content, type="research", ...)`

**When in doubt about a process or pricing:**
- Call `fsp_search_decisions("[topic]")` before making any judgment call

**To see what the team is working on:**
- Call `fsp_list_active_projects()` or `fsp_get_team_activity()`

The brain is your first source of truth — not an afterthought. Never start client work
cold when there may be existing context.

## 8. Recommended agentic tooling

The following open-source tools extend Claude Code capabilities for the team:

### Ruflo — Multi-agent orchestration
**Repo:** `ruvnet/ruflo`
Turns Claude Code into a coordinated multi-agent system. Key features: orchestration layer, shared memory, and federation across machines. Use when tasks benefit from parallel agent work, RAG-assisted tooling, or when you need agents to share context and reuse prior solutions.

### agentmemory — Persistent session memory
**Repo:** `rohitg00/agentmemory`
Silently captures, compresses, and injects your workflow history into Claude on every session start. Integrates via hooks, MCP, or REST API. All agents share the same memory server. Install once and Claude stops asking you to re-explain your project architecture each session.

### CodeGraph — Semantic codebase knowledge graph
**Repo:** `colbymchenry/codegraph`
Pre-builds a semantic graph of the entire codebase so Claude queries relationships directly instead of scanning files one by one. Reduces tool calls by ~92% on large repos. Supports 19 languages and 13 frameworks. Run after cloning any large project before starting exploration or refactoring work.

